# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.sileolists -- Sileo's queue and the working directory apt sees.
#
# Sileo empties the queue in reloadData(recheckPackages:)'s catch: recheckTotalOps()
# runs as root `apt-get -sqf ... -oDir::State::lists=sileolists/ install --reinstall
# <pkg>=<ver>`.  The lists path is relative and Sileo never chdir()s (spawnAsRoot sets
# only PATH), so it resolves against whatever directory the root spawn inherits -- "/"
# if nothing sets one.  The scene plants the one-line answer at "/" and then prints
# the same apt query from both directories, so the hypothesis is settled even if the
# queue never takes.
#
# The GET is tapped twice at most and then nothing else touches the screen: Sileo's
# own error alert (if it comes) must survive to a frame instead of being tapped away.
/redwood/bin/sleep_hold 600 &
/var/jb/bin/sh /var/jb/prep.sh
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 120 joinfile /redwood/fw/network
/redwood/bin/net_test waitaddr en0 60 resolve apt.procurs.us
/var/jb/usr/bin/apt-get update
/var/jb/bin/sh /redwood/bin/sileo-seed.sh
/var/jb/usr/bin/ln -sfn /var/jb/var/lib/apt/sileolists /sileolists
/var/jb/bin/sh /redwood/bin/sileolists-probe.sh
# A sileo:// URL that starts Sileo from cold only opens the Featured page (the same way a
# prefs: URL lands on the Settings root): launch it first, let it settle, then send the deep
# link to the package page.  The 2026-11-19 01:22 frames show Sileo on Featured and the taps
# that followed landing in TrollStore instead.
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen sileo://
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 30
# Two things stand between the launch and the package page, and neither was answered before:
# the notification alert (Don't Allow at 0.32 0.59) and Sileo's own analytics consent
# ("Download Analytics", Provided by Canister: Accept is the full-width button at about
# 0.5 0.90, Deny above it at 0.835).  The 2026-11-19 01:39 frame shows Sileo sitting on that
# consent screen while the scene tapped where GET would be.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.32 0.59 wait 6
# Deny, not Accept: 0.90 is close enough to the home indicator that the tap was read as the
# home gesture and dismissed Sileo (quiet3-13 is the home screen right after it).
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.5 0.835 wait 10
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen sileo://package/tree
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 30 tap 0.86 0.37 wait 10
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 20 tap 0.86 0.37 wait 15
# The queue is filled by the taps above (both 2026-11-19 runs show Sileo's apt simulation
# twice), but the scene had no step after them.  The package page is a sheet with no Done
# button, and the popup bar that opens the downloads sheet sits behind it: close the sheet
# with the grabber drag the 2026-11-13 runs measured (its top edge is at about 0.06 of the
# screen), then tap the bar just above the tab bar (0.885, with 0.90/0.87 as the misses
# either side) and Confirm in the downloads sheet's footer (0.93/0.88/0.84).
# No swipe from the top edge: on this system the top edge is the Notification Centre / Cover
# Sheet gesture, and the 2026-11-19 02:17 run's swipe landed the phone on the lock screen
# (quiet6-24) with every later tap on it.
# The package page's own menu is the "..." at its top right (about 0.908 0.09); Sileo's
# binary carries downloadsButton/downloadsController, so the downloads sheet is reachable from
# there without closing the page.  This run only opens that menu and leaves it for the camera:
# the item's position is not known yet.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch notify com.hakios.close-sheet wait 10
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.908 0.09 wait 12
# (The bar tap at 0.5 0.885 and the Confirm taps at 0.93/0.88/0.84 follow once the menu item's
# position is measured: tapping them into an open menu could hit anything in it.)
/var/jb/bin/sh /redwood/bin/sileolists-probe.sh
/var/jb/usr/bin/dpkg-query -W -f=${binary:Package}_${Version}_${Status}\n tree
/var/jb/usr/bin/ls -la /var/jb/usr/bin/tree
